Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["1d single-point evaluation (OneDfunctional.wl)", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"65d1cba3-ada3-4dea-8d22-1936b08e7508"],

Cell["\<\
The lowest layer of the package: the 1d crossing functionals evaluated at a \
single point. These are the building blocks that generate1ptmx (next section) \
tabulates over a \[CapitalDelta] grid. After loading, the OneDfunctional` \
symbols are on the context path \[LongDash] no qualification needed.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"78f7c6ca-4c7a-46d9-9dc1-abfaf03347a8"],

Cell["Get[FileNameJoin[{NotebookDirectory[], \"FunTable.wl\"}]]", "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "7/23/26 11:36:40 \
In[5]:=",ExpressionUUID->"cc1887ba-557f-4e80-adbe-6805f2cc3f06"],

Cell["\<\
Arguments are (\[CapitalDelta]\[Phi], m, \[CapitalDelta]): external \
dimension, functional order m, operator dimension \[CapitalDelta]. The option \
PrecisionGoal sets the working precision (default 150). Use exact rationals. \
Example point: \[CapitalDelta]\[Phi] = 0.26, m = 2, \[CapitalDelta] = 2.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c81921bd-a5c7-4fc9-9eaa-229b3a47b8f6"],

Cell["dphi = 3/5; m = 2; d = 2;", "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9938096815781097`*^9, 3.99380968417181*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "7/23/26 11:36:41 \
In[6]:=",ExpressionUUID->"3f24aca1-6c22-4132-a54c-5d5584d53586"],

