Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Usage example \[LongDash] generating a 3d functional table (.h5)", \
"Section",ExpressionUUID->"e6b2421c-a396-4cee-868c-512f2e23d717"],

Cell["\<\
Self-contained walk-through of the generation pipeline (current API). The \
sections below this one are the original working scratchpad.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f08410ff-8bc1-4f58-84b4-fbb2b3c8aac4"],

Cell["\<\
Load the package. Get it as a FILE so $InputFileName resolves the src/ paths:\
\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e7ec388f-db40-409c-a58d-88d761735190"],

Cell["Get[FileNameJoin[{NotebookDirectory[], \"FunTable.wl\"}]]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"259da16f-253a-4f73-a987-5e8234ea10dc"],

Cell["\<\
Launch parallel kernels \[LongDash] the 1d generation step uses ParallelMap:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"fb78c24a-a3b3-4abc-abaf-6d5847e7fc86"],

Cell["LaunchKernels[]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"c1bfd414-86d9-48e9-91b5-66db8de344fe"],

Cell["\<\
Choose the external dimension as an EXACT rational (avoids float rounding in \
the high-precision generation). Convention: dphi1d = \
\[CapitalDelta]\[Phi](3d)/2. The example is the 3d Ising point.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"063e3b02-34ce-47e6-ac35-0d1c9e29cbf8"],

Cell["\<\
dphi3d = 5181488023/10000000000;
dphi1d = dphi3d/2;\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"33cde921-a702-4d8e-9f8c-03a1d35315e2"],

Cell["\<\
Generation parameters. VeryHigh: dmaxgen=650, nmax=500 (High: 500, 350). \
orderMax is the functional truncation order (10 standard, 12 extended).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"301f6156-aadd-4498-9df5-0c2ae7edba76"],

Cell["\<\
orderMax = 10; order = 10;
spinlist = Range[0, 100, 2];
dmax = 150; dmaxgen = 650; nmax = 500;\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"d28a981a-fd85-4ff5-9743-b46814bce0db"],

Cell["\<\
Step 1 \[LongDash] build the 1d table (.mx). The trailing True enables the \
exp-only normalization: the functionals are built at high precision, then \
rescaled by 2^(-2\[CapitalDelta]) before conversion to machine reals to avoid \
4^\[CapitalDelta] overflow at large \[CapitalDelta].\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3bcb07a9-c618-458d-a44f-b8f095530cd8"],

Cell["\<\
generate1ptmx[\"Ising10.mx\", dphi1d, orderMax, dmaxgen, True];\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"e46851d2-d844-4621-bd93-b70e74c54afc"],

Cell["\<\
Step 2 \[LongDash] build the 3d functional table from the 1d .mx. \
\"normed\"->True applies the standard normalization; \"fill\"->30 fills the \
30 grid points just below each spin's unitarity bound \[CapitalDelta]\
\[GreaterEqual]\[ScriptL]+1 with the analytic continuation (ghost nodes, used \
only as interpolation support; \"fill\"->0 reproduces the classic \
\[CapitalDelta]\[GreaterEqual]\[ScriptL]+1 table).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e5c62ec7-d19f-4512-b497-1e0040b97c22"],

Cell["\<\
lp = init3DTablePatch[\"Ising10.mx\", order, spinlist, dmax, nmax, \"normed\" \
-> True, \"fill\" -> 30];\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"0fc67a9c-ec89-469f-b1f7-d6628c4444e8"],

Cell["\<\
Step 3 \[LongDash] export to HDF5: rename the \[CapitalDelta]table key to \
dtable and drop the internal normed flag (the LP loader's schema).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4c932d87-6508-4b0c-b223-b8efa531c61c"],

Cell["\<\
lpNew = KeyDrop[KeyMap[# /. \"\[CapitalDelta]table\" -> \"dtable\" &, lp], \
\"normed\"];
Export[\"Ising10.h5\", Normal[lpNew], \"HDF5\"];\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"13efe943-7530-4ad4-a936-e3a60b86a910"],

Cell["\<\
Notes. (1) 1d dphi = 3d \[CapitalDelta]\[Phi] / 2. (2) Grids: 1d Range[0, \
dmaxgen, 1/202]; 2d/3d spacing 1/101 (halfstep = 101), index i \
\[LongLeftRightArrow] \[CapitalDelta] = (i-1)/101. (3) Packed table dims \
{nspins, n\[CapitalDelta], funcnum}; each row is \[CapitalDelta]=0 (spin 0 \
only), zero for 0<\[CapitalDelta]<\[ScriptL]+1-fill/101, populated above. (4) \
Special dphi: 3d \[CapitalDelta]\[Phi]=3/2 (1d 3/4) is handled in-source; 3d \
\[CapitalDelta]\[Phi]=1 (1d 1/2) requires evaluating dphi at \
SetPrecision[dphi,200]+10^-30.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"084d0418-71d6-43dd-bde3-330384d46206"]
}, Open  ]]
},
